Topic: Difference between Process and Service in linux 

1.A process is any running program.
2.A service is a special kind of process:
Long-running
Background
Usually started automatically
Managed by the OS (via systemd, init.d, etc.)

Eample 
# Viewing a process
ps aux | grep python

# Managing a service
systemctl status nginx
systemctl restart sshd

A service is a managed background process that can auto-start and restart, while a regular process needs to be manually managed.
